WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.102
-Thank you so much for tuning in
and watching our show.

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.804
My name is Jimmy Fallon.
That is The Roots right there.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.773
This is The Roots.

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:10.943
I saw your face light up when
you heard Higgins say

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:12.378
"Buju Banton."

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:15.848
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Very excited about that.

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:19.352
Alright, let's get to the news
and jokes right now.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:22.422
Guys, the Democratic National
Convention continued tonight,

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:25.792
but everyone's still talking
about Michelle Obama's speech.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:28.061
She really brought the heat,
especially when she used

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.796
President Trump's
own words against him.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.130
Watch this.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.334 line:0%
-Donald Trump is the wrong
president for our country.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:39.538 line:0%
He has had more than enough time
to prove that he can do the job,

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:42.942 line:0%
but he is clearly
in over his head.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.144 line:0%
He cannot meet this moment.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:50.383 line:0%
He simply cannot be
who we need him to be for us.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.152 line:0%
It is what it is.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:55.388 line:0%
-Ooh!

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.956
At that point, Trump squeezed
his Diet Coke hand so hard,

00:00:57.956 --> 00:01:00.760
it turned into a diamond.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.161
I'm serious.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.163
Right after that, a doctor took
Trump's blood pressure,

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:08.634
and the cuff exploded.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.770
I always get scared of
those machines at CVS,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.539
'cause I don't necessarily trust
that they know

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:14.940
what they're doing, the robots.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.610
-Wait. You take that test?
-Yeah, I'm bored. I'm waiting.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.678
What am I supposed to do?
I got to --

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.647
-You know, like, they sell --

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:23.082
You can just get
your own machine.

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:24.917
-I don't want to have
more stuff.

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:25.985
I don't need more stuff.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.721
CVS has a giant one with
the arm sleeve.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.423
And it's like,
I'm the guy in the mall

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:33.159
that gets, you know,
massaged in the chair.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.194
-While they shop.
-That's me, yeah.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.763
-Yeah, stick your arm in -- Aah!

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.397
-No, I just -- It kept going.
And it was like...

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.233
[ Imitates whooshing ]

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.335
And then you're
like, "This could be broke."

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:45.138
And then -- I mean, should my
face be turning red?

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.308
Like, how tight does
this cuff...

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.842
How, like, accurate
is my blood pressure?

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:55.748
It's like, "No, it's 8,624.
That sounds like a good number."

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.517
We don't have footage of
the moment Trump

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.485
heard Michelle Obama say,
"It is what it is,"

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:02.021
but I imagine it
resembled something like this.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:05.891
♪♪
-Nooooo!

00:02:05.891 --> 00:02:08.327
-Yeah, that's right --
everyone is saying

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:10.563
the former First Lady
stole the night.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:13.066
I'm actually worried the speech
might have backfired for Biden,

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.466
because right after,
everyone with a ballot

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:17.136
wrote in "Michelle Obama."

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.804
Well, this morning,
while at an event for

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:21.507
the 100th anniversary of
the 19th Amendment,

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.409
Trump was asked about
Michelle Obama's speech,

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.610
and here's what he had to say.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:25.678
Listen to this.

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:33.986
Oh, yeah.
That's a good comeback.

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:36.822
Trump said, "She was --
You're in over your head."

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:40.025
That was her insult against you.
You can't use her insult.

00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:41.794
Every third grader
who can't go back to school

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.831
knows you can't do that.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:45.932
Oh, and did you hear about this?

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.767
At the same event for the
19th Amendment,

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.735
Trump decided to make
a surprise announcement.

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:50.736
Check it out.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:53.039
-Later today, I will be signing

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:57.677
a full and complete pardon
for Susan B. Anthony.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:03:01.414
-Yeah. There's --
-Wait, what?

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.883
-There's no bigger champion
for women than the man

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.417
who spent his morning
rage-tweeting

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:08.121
about Michelle Obama.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:12.225
Trump pardoned Susan B. Anthony,
who died in 1906.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.961
He was like,
"Sadly, she died in 1906

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.029
from the Spanish flu of 1917,

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:19.031
right at the end of
World War II,

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:23.068
which, of course, was in 1969."

00:03:23.068 --> 00:03:25.070
Yep, Trump pardoned
Susan B. Anthony.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:29.275
Then he complained that
she didn't thank him.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.376
But back to the convention.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.311
Last night,
Bernie Sanders also spoke,

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:33.846
and this moment
went pretty viral.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:34.847
Watch this.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:38.751 line:0%
-Nero fiddled while Rome burned.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.686 line:0%
Trump golfs.

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:44.090
-Yeah. Bernie was like,
"Trust me about Rome.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.726
I was there."

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:49.462
Also, look at all that
wood he's got.

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:52.030
Man, when they told Bernie
to log on to the event,

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.667
he took it literally.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:04:00.640
[ As Sanders ]
I have 800 logs ready.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.008
[ Normal voice ] Actually,
that wasn't firewood.

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:04.077
It turns out Bernie makes
his own teeth.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:07.313
No, come on. Hey.
That's not true.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.415
Well, after a big opening night,
the Democrats

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.516
were back at it again today.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:11.817 line:0%
Check it out.

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:14.286 line:0%
-It's Day 2 of the
Democratic National Convention.

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:16.255 line:0%
Here are some of the voices
you'll hear tonight --

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:17.857 line:0%
former president Bill Clinton,

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.359 line:0%
Congresswoman
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez,

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:22.027 line:0%
and Dr. Jill Biden.

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:23.996
-Yeah, former president
Bill Clinton spoke tonight.

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:25.297
And this was fun.

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:27.233
During the speech, you could see
Hillary in the background

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:32.238
throwing uppercuts
at frozen slabs of meat.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:34.540
There was a scary moment midway
through tonight's program,

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.976
when they realized they forgot
to pick up John Kasich

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:41.080
from the middle of that old
country road he was standing on.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.182
"Someone send help!"

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.551
But this is interesting --
former president Jimmy Carter

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.387
also spoke tonight.

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:48.721
That's how old Joe Biden is.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:54.226
They brought in Jimmy Carter
to rally the youth vote.

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:55.861
Meanwhile, the Republicans
are busy planning

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:57.463
their convention for next week.

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.131
And everyone is wondering who
Trump will invite

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:01.934
to compete against all those
popular Democratic speakers.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.603 line:0%
-As for the Republican National
Convention next week,

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:07.340 line:0%
a St. Louis couple accused
of pointing guns at protesters

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.609 line:0%
outside their home will be
speaking at the event.

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:12.945 line:0%
That's from an aide
familiar with the plans.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:16.949
-Seriously? He invited them?

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.785
Democrats are featuring
first responders, virus victims,

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:22.255
anti-racism activists, while
Trump was like,

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:25.758
"Who went viral
for something dumb?

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:28.427
Is Jake Paul available?"

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:31.196
But the RNC has some other
big plans for the event.

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:32.198
Check this out.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.599 line:0%
-The Republican National
Committee

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:38.137 line:0%
has filed a permit for fireworks
at the Washington Monument

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:41.574 line:0%
to celebrate Trump's expected
renomination acceptance speech.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.443
-Trump settled on fireworks
at the Washington Monument

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.045
after they told him
it was impossible

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:50.516
to have lasers shoot out of
the eyes on Mount Rushmore.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.752
[ As Trump ] How impossible?

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:54.820
Really impossible?

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.555
Just double-checking.

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.123
[ Normal voice ] But if they
can't get the fireworks permit,

00:05:58.123 --> 00:05:59.992
Trump's going to have
the couple from St. Louis

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:03.095
fire a few rounds into the sky.

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:05.030
Well, guys, earlier today,
Louis DeJoy,

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:08.100
the postmaster general
of the USPS,

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.134
made a pretty big announcement.

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:10.503 line:0%
Listen to this.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:13.506 line:0%
-Facing immense bipartisan
pressure and public outcry,

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:15.675 line:0%
DeJoy announced
he will delay many of his

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:20.046 line:0%
controversial changes to the
USPS until after the election.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.713
-Man, Trump almost got
away with it.

00:06:21.713 --> 00:06:22.915
The only time he slipped up was

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:25.484
when he revealed
his entire plan on national TV.

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.619
Other than that, flawless.

00:06:27.619 --> 00:06:28.954
Check this out.

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:30.956
I saw that a company in Japan
has figured out a way

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:33.059
to make a haunted house
while maintaining

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.159
social distancing.

00:06:34.159 --> 00:06:35.294 line:0%
Check this out.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.230 line:0%
-A haunted-house company
in Japan will soon offer

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:41.300 line:0%
a drive-in haunted house
to keep the scares going.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.868 line:0%
The owner said he got the idea

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:44.604 line:0%
from drive-in movie theaters.

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:47.106
-Yeah, that's smart --
jump-scaring people

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:49.409
while they have their foot
on the gas.

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:54.346
It's the only haunted house

00:06:54.346 --> 00:06:56.148
that's scarier for
the performers.

00:06:56.148 --> 00:06:57.983
It's like...

00:06:57.983 --> 00:06:59.384
And, finally, listen to this.

00:06:59.384 --> 00:07:02.187
The other day, a glitch at a
chocolate factory in Switzerland

00:07:02.187 --> 00:07:05.357
caused an entire town to be
dusted in cocoa.

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:07.826
America's in the throes
of a pandemic,

00:07:07.826 --> 00:07:09.561
racial upheaval,
and a recession.

00:07:09.561 --> 00:07:11.263
Meanwhile, Europe is like,
"Oh, no.

00:07:11.263 --> 00:07:14.867
Ze town is covered in
chocolate."

